Reading some of the more negative reviews I felt obligated to say I love where the game is so far. It's like Terraria except expanded upon. Sure, they've gotten rid of or changed some features from before 1.0, but look at Terraria. It's been out since 2011, had an update last week, and people still play it (ignoring the Terraria otherworld and Terraria 2 announcements). Starbound's full version just came out two months ago and they added a 1.1 patch to the game so it's not like the developers just dropped everything and said "We're done! There's nothing else we could possibly add to make this game better!"
If you check in with their dev blog on their website (
) you might find the feature or update you've been expecting after a while. And if you still don't like what they've done with it after a few patches then look for mods! To quote their website "You have the tools to make the universe your own and modify the game to suit your play style - add new races, biomes, dungeons, and quests - the possibilities are limitless". The developers purposely made the game easily moddable because they support and understand the creative abilities of their fans (They even share mods they find with each other).
So despite the negative reviews, I love how this game came out and if I find myself not enjoying the base game I can rely on other people with their mods or learn how to mod this mod friendly game myself. I'm positive, though, that the developers will continue to make it even better by listening to the things people post on their forums (which you should go to if you want to really complain or make a suggestion -->
) as well as relying on their own creative mindsets that brought us this great game in the first place.
